
1. Read an INI File
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file and displays all configuration 
sections available in the file.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.sections()

2. Check Whether a Section Exists
Program:Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, checks whether a section named 
database exists, and prints an appropriate message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.has_section()

3. Check Whether a Key Exists
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, checks whether the key host 
exists in the database section, and prints the result.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.has_option()

4. Read a Specific Configuration Value
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file and displays the value of the 
host key from the database section.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.get()

5. Add a New Section
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, adds a new section named 
application, saves the changes, and prints a success message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.add_section()
config.write()

6. Add a New Key and Value

Program:

Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, adds a key named version with value 1.0 to the application section, saves the file, and prints a success message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.set()
config.write()

7. Update an Existing Value
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, changes the value of the host key 
in the database section to dbserver, writes the changes back to the file, and displays a confirmation message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.set()
config.write()

8. Remove a Key from a Section
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, removes the key user from the database section, saves the updated file, and prints a success message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.remove_option()
config.write()

9. Remove an Entire Section
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that reads an existing app.ini file, removes the server section completely, saves the changes, and displays a confirmation message.

Methods Covered:
config.read()
config.remove_section()
config.write()

10. Create a Complete Configuration File
Program: Write a Python program using the configparser module that creates a new file named config.ini, adds two sections named database and server, adds appropriate keys and values to each section, writes the configuration to disk, and prints a success message.

Methods Covered:

config.add_section()
config.set()
config.write()


Complete Learning Order
Read INI file (read)
List sections (sections)
Check section (has_section)
Check key (has_option)
Read value (get)
Add section (add_section)
Add/Update value (set)
Remove key (remove_option)
Remove section (remove_section)
Save changes (write)

These 10 programs cover nearly all day-to-day configparser usage for DevOps, Linux administration, and automation scripts.
